{"id":"e6932924-09aa-4ca6-b198-2f8081cc8b1c","object":"chat.completion","created":1784995853,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    core = case[\\\"core_distance\\\"]\\n    distances = case[\\\"distances\\\"]\\n    edges = []\\n    seen = set()\\n    for d in distances:\\n        u, v, w = d\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        key = (u, v)\\n        if key in seen:\\n            continue\\n        seen.add(key)\\n        mut_dist = max(core[u], core[v], w)\\n        edges.append((mut_dist, u, v))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    parent = {n: n for n in nodes}\\n    rank = {n: 0 for n in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Graph is disconnected\\\")\\n    return {\\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges, \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to generate Python code for solve(case) that satisfies the output schema. The task: Given nodes list, core_distance dict, and distances list (each a 3-element list [node1, node2, distance]), compute mutual reachability distances: max(core_left, core_right, distance). Then construct a minimum spanning tree using Kruskal's algorithm. For deterministic behavior, we need to sort edges by weight, then by endpoint IDs (presumably lexicographically or by canonical order). Union-find with path compression and union by rank. Must handle disconnected case? The description says \"Reject disconnected inputs\" so we raise ValueError if we can't connect all nodes. The output must have mst_edges and total_weight. mst_edges is a list of arrays each [string, string, number] with exactly 3 elements. The output schema requires items: array with prefixItems: [string, string, number], and additionalProperties false, but the items array itself is free? Actually the schema says items: { type: array, minItems:3, maxItems:3, prefixItems: [...]}. That means each edge is a 3-element array. total_weight is number.\n\nWe need to implement solve(case) that returns such a dict. The input case is the payload (the inner object). It contains \"nodes\", \"core_distance\", \"distances\". \"nodes\" is list of node ids (strings). \"distances\" is list of [node1, node2, distance]. We assume all distances are symmetric? Possibly but we should handle both directions. The mutual reachability is symmetric: max(core[a], core[b], dist). We'll consider each unordered pair once by canonicalizing (sort node ids). Then sort edges by weight, then by node1, then node2. Then Kruskal. Use union-find with dictionary mapping node to parent/rank. We need to ensure all nodes are connected; if after processing all edges we have less than n-1 edges, raise ValueError.\n\nReturn {\"mst_edges\": edges, \"total_weight\": sum(weights)}.\n\nEdge cases: duplicates? Not expected but we can handle. The distances list might not be exhaustive? But we assume enough to form a graph.\n\nWe'll implement as a function solve(case). We'll not import anything beyond standard library. Use only Python built-ins.\n\nNow produce the JSON with key \"implementation\" containing the code as a string. Escape properly. We'll output the JSON object with exactly that key.\n\nLet's write the code:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    core = case[\"core_distance\"]\n    distances = case[\"distances\"]\n    # Build adjacency? Actually just edges list.\n    # Build list of (weight, u, v) for unique undirected edges.\n    edges = []\n    seen = set()\n    for d in distances:\n        u, v, w = d\n        # Canonical order: ensure u < v? but they are strings, use sorted?\n        # \"Canonicalize undirected endpoints\": sort by node id string.\n        if u > v:\n            u, v = v, u\n        key = (u, v)\n        if key in seen:\n            continue\n        seen.add(key)\n        # Compute mutual reachability distance\n        mut_dist = max(core[u], core[v], w)\n        edges.append((mut_dist, u, v))\n    # Sort by weight, then by u, then by v\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\n    # Union-find\n    parent = {n: n for n in nodes}\n    rank = {n: 0 for n in nodes}\n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\n            parent[rx] = ry\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n        else:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    mst_edges = []\n    total_weight = 0.0\n    for w, u, v in edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\n            total_weight += w\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\n                break\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Graph is disconnected\")\n    return {\"mst_edges\": mst_edges, \"total_weight\": total_weight}\n\nThat should work. Ensure no mutation of input. The code uses only standard lib.\n\nNow stringify it with proper JSON escaping. We'll output the JSON.\n\nMake sure the response is exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value a string containing the Python code. No extra text.\n\nWe'll produce the final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2017,"completion_tokens":1548,"total_tokens":3565,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1084},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":97},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}